      "item_body": "<p>[K/U] The graph of the function y = f(x) is shown at the left.</p>\n<p>a. Estimate the intervals on which the function is increasing.</p>\n<p>b. Estimate the intervals on which f'(x) &lt; 0.</p>\n<p>c. Estimate the coordinates of the critical points of f.</p>\n<p>d. Estimate the equations of any vertical asymptotes of the function.</p>\n<p>e. What is the value (sign) of f''(x) on the interval -4 &lt; x &lt; 4?</p>\n<p>f. If x &gt;= -6, estimate the intervals on which f'(x) &lt; 0 and f''(x) &gt; 0.</p>\n<p>g. Identify a point of inflection on the graph and give its approximate ordered pair.</p>\n<p><img src=\"https://inst-fs-iad-prod.inscloudgate.net/files/23eb30a8-f45f-4805-bab9-1a267ad67896/test_q1.png?token=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzUxMiIsImtpZCI6Im5ldy1xdWl6emVzL21haW4ifQ..h8gei5138nn5tff9-svv4vkaLsMbtiMRYRVx_39ivVZKHR8LOKIhG_yPcVtjie5V1IukfpExkm_M-AuF4GEGwA\" alt=\"Nelson Calculus and Vectors 12, Ch 4, p. 220 - Chapter 4 Test, Question 1: graph of y = f(x)\" width=\"100%\" height=\"100%\" data-old-link=\"https://bronston.instructure.com/courses/905/files/55759/preview\"></p>\n<p>a. increasing: <span id=\"blank_0f77b374-3ead-40ba-9591-a0fa0d543f9c\"></span></p>\n<p>b. f'(x) &lt; 0: <span id=\"blank_05a9539f-f573-4372-aa04-18db719b2c5f\"></span></p>\n<p>c. critical points: <span id=\"blank_0255aace-e57c-4602-ade0-1facbdc36a4c\"></span>, <span id=\"blank_90edd0dc-f1d9-4c0d-b0e1-3540e5ebb314\"></span>, <span id=\"blank_278906f4-5947-46c5-a462-47b8dbc97210\"></span>, and <span id=\"blank_7560085b-fdaf-4667-9602-30ce38f8f5b2\"></span></p>\n<p>d. vertical asymptotes: <span id=\"blank_76974a94-3f54-48e9-bf14-6d4d44aeee8c\"></span> and <span id=\"blank_bc38322a-45f9-427e-9a7f-e7cff5ee5628\"></span></p>\n<p>e. on -4 &lt; x &lt; 4, f''(x) is <span id=\"blank_b7886ded-b2a6-4896-94be-a2ac4e7022ac\"></span></p>\n<p>f. f'(x) &lt; 0 and f''(x) &gt; 0: <span id=\"blank_5587fbbf-8eae-4f7a-81a6-785ac3e9619c\"></span></p>\n<p>g. a point of inflection: <s